# Commit and PR messages

Engineering artifacts are **English** unless the user asks otherwise. This rule applies when writing a commit or PR message (`CM`, `PR`, `GACM`, `CBol`).

## Commit

`<prefix>(<scope>): <imperative summary>`

Prefixes: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`.
Scopes: `reviews`, `replies`, `channels`, `auth`, `ui`, `context`.

```
feat(reviews): list pending reviews for the active hotel
fix(replies): reject publish when the review belongs to another hotel
docs(context): document the home screen schema
```

## Pull request

When the user asks for a PR message (`PR`), output title + body only unless they also asked to open the PR.

1. `Summary` — 1–2 sentences
2. `What Changed` — short bullets
3. `Security Notes` — always present; say “none” if none
